practice.stem:
A stylesheet contains:
body { background-color: #FFFFFF; font-family: Georgia, serif; }
.note { color: #8B0000; font-weight: bold; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 90%; }
td { border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 6px; }

parts.text:
Write CSS rules so that:
• every table is 75% of the width of the window and its borders are collapsed into single lines;
• every th and td cell has a 1-pixel solid border in #333333 and 8 pixels of padding.

Write the complete head section of a web page that:
• uses the character set UTF-8;
• has the title 'Margalla Garden Centre';
• has the description 'Plants and seeds delivered across Islamabad';
• attaches the stylesheet garden.css, which is in a folder called css.

practice.stem:
The head of a web page contains:
<link rel="stylesheet" href="main.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="summer.css">
main.css contains: p { color: #000000; font-size: 11pt; }
summer.css contains: p { color: #FF4500; }
One paragraph is written as <p style="font-size: 14pt;">Summer sale now on.</p>

parts.text:
A stylesheet contains the rule:
body { font-family: "Segoe UI", Tahoma, sans-serif; }
Explain why "Segoe UI" is written in quotation marks and why three fonts are listed in this order.

A stylesheet contains these rules:
h2 { colour: #1A5276; text-align: centre; font-size 20px }
p { font-family: Arial sans-serif; }
Identify and correct the four errors.

A Frequently Asked Questions page has three level 2 headings: 'How do I apply?', 'What documents are needed?' and 'When are results announced?'. Write the HTML for:
• the three headings, each with a suitable id (no spaces);
• a bulleted list at the top of the page in which each item is a link that jumps to the matching heading.

Write the CSS rules for an external stylesheet that:
• sets the page background colour to #FAF0E6 and the font to Georgia, with serif as the generic fallback;
• makes h1 headings #2F4F4F, 32px and centre aligned.

Add rules to the same stylesheet that:
• make h2 headings 18pt, right aligned and bold;
• create a class called note that makes text #B22222 and italic.

A student has inserted a photograph into a two-column report. The teacher notes these problems:
• the photograph looks squashed;
• it overlaps the right margin by 1 cm;
• the text stops above the photograph and starts again below it, leaving large empty spaces at the sides;
• the top of the photograph covers part of the header.
For each problem, describe how the student should correct it.
